.SS "double csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTriangle::dN_AtIntegrationPoint (\fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & B, uint32_t gauss_point)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.IP "1." 4
Pre-multiplies local interpolation function derivative matrix, B, with node coordinates to obtain the Jacobian matrix, J\&.
.IP "2." 4
The Jacobian matrix J is inverted and multiplied with B to obtain the global interpolation function derivative matrix at the gauss point i (i=0\&.\&.\&.i=gauss points-1)\&. If a transformation from 2D local to 3D global space is applied, the function Jacobi is called\&.
.PP
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The first argument is a reference to the parent \fBElement\fP object, the second argument is the result matrix, the third argument indicates the gauss point at which the derivative matrix is computed and the fourth argument specifies the degrees of freedom per node, for which the B matrix shall be transformed\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIB\fP The global interpolation function derivative matrix is returned into the second method argument\&. The method also returns the determinant of the Jacobian matrix since it is often needed in integration procedures\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::FiniteElement\fP\&.
.SS "double csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTriangle::dN_AtNode (\fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & B, uint32_t nd)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.IP "1." 4
Pre-multiplies local interpolation function derivative matrix, B, with node coordinates to obtain the Jacobian matrix, J at the desired node point\&.
.IP "2." 4
The Jacobian matrix J is inverted and multiplied with B to obtain the global interpolation function derivative matrix at the point i (i=0\&.\&.\&.i=gauss points-1)\&. If a transformation from 2D local to 3D global space is applied, the function Jacobi is called\&.
.PP
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The first argument is a reference to the parent \fBElement\fP object, the second argument is the result matrix, the third argument indicates the gauss point at which the derivative matrix is computed and the fourth argument specifies the degrees of freedom per node, for which the B matrix shall be transformed\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The global interpolation function derivative matrix is returned into the second method argument\&. The method also returns the determinant of the Jacobian matrix since it is often needed in integration procedures\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::FiniteElement\fP\&.
.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTriangle::dNr (double s, double t, std::vector< double > & DNR) const\fR [virtual]\fP"
This method and the complementary method \fBdNs()\fP compute the shape function derivates with respect to the local coordinate axis 'r', and 's'\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The method takes the local coordinates of the point at which the shape function derivatives shall be evaluated as third argument\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIDNR\fP The shape function derivatives are returned into the second method argument which is a Meschpp floating point vector of the size n=nodes per element\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
see inlined source code in the header file\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The shape function derivatives are needed in most integration procedures for elements\&. 
