.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTriangle::OutputNodeDataToVTK (const char * file_name, const char * var_name, \fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & DATA) const\fR [virtual]\fP"
Method returns a vector with a size of 3, containing the consecutively ordered local node numbers of the side of the element which lies at the indicated model boundary\&. If the element is not on the model boundary an error is reported and the vector is initialized to unspecified\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The parent \fBElement\fP, the target boundary of the the \fBModel\fP of elements, and a Meschach vector which will hold the the local indices of the identified nodes (0\&.\&.\&.5)\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfnids\fP The resulting local node id's are returned into the third method argument\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
While only the element knows which nodes are located at the mode boundary, the \fBFiniteElement\fP knows in which order these appear\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To assign Neumann boundary conditions with a PDE operator for surface integrals\&. Outputs nodal values of a triangle into user-specified output file\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The parent element, the output file name to which the extension "\&.vtk" will be appended automatically, the name of the variable, a data matrix which will contain n-colums=nodes and n-rows = dimensions of data (n-rows=1 = scalar data, n-rows=3 = vector data etc\&.)\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Single elements are output to VTK as polygons in order to test the quality of interpolation and the computed properties directly\&.
.SH "Messages"
